  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, thanks for reaching out. You're right: Duo was never set up on your account, so the VPN can't finish signing you in. Your account and new laptop both look fine, and setup is quick. You and a technician will do it together in a short session (remote or in person), because you'll need your phone to scan a code. To get ready: 1) On your phone, install the free 'Duo Mobile' app from the App Store or Google Play. 2) Reply with a few times that work for you for a 15-minute session during your usual 9 to 5 Eastern hours, and say whether you'd like remote or in person. During the session the technician will check the Duo software on your laptop, help you scan the code, and send a test notification to make sure it works. The VPN won't work until this is done. If you need something urgently before then, please tell us.",
  "internal_note": "Sender verified as the account owner (sent from her own email). Hannah Lee, user 12, Finance Payroll Specialist, not VIP, ET 09:00-17:00. Account: active, sign-in not blocked, VPN access true, 0 failed logins. Password set 2026-10-11 with must_change_password=true, which fits a new-hire or new-laptop setup. MFA check: enrolled=false, no device, so Duo was never set up. Laptop BL-LT-0112 (Win 11) is online, last check-in 2026-10-11 03:05 UTC, 51% disk free, no warnings. Sign-in logs: 10 successful sign-ins, all from New York on corporate or residential networks, during her usual hours, mfa=none, including VPN successes up to 10/08. That suggests Duo enforcement on VPN started recently or came with the new laptop. No failed attempts, no MFA denials, no hosting-network IPs, so nothing points to a compromise. Per KB-004 the fix is a scheduled enrollment session with the user present: she installs Duo Mobile, we install the Duo client on BL-LT-0112 if it's missing, she scans the activation QR code, then we send a test push. I asked her for availability and whether she wants remote or in person. A technician needs to book and run the session. Until then she can't use VPN. No action tools used.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-004",
    "KB-013"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
